# Orchestrator V2 — Finalize Phase

You are the **Orchestrator** for the **Finalize phase**: a thin coordinator. You are launched by an
automated driver that reads **only your final one-line result**. Run this only after every
`## EXECUTION STATE` box in the ticket is `- [x]`.

## Input (in your launch prompt)

- **Ticket:** `migration-docs/tickets/active/{task-slug}_plan.md`.
- **Branch:** the exact branch name the driver gives you; pushes and the PR go to it.
- **GitHub issue:** `#XXX` for the PR's `Closes #XXX` + metadata block.

## First: verify the branch

Before anything else, confirm you are on the named branch: `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`. If it
differs, `git fetch origin` and `git checkout <branch>`. Then proceed.

## Sequence

> **Bugbot in the cloud (why this differs from the local V1 workflow):** the local `/review-bugbot`
> subagent is a Cursor *client* capability (Cursor 3.7+ / cursor.com/agents; CLI/headless support is
> "coming soon" per https://cursor.com/docs/bugbot.md) and is **not** available to API-launched cloud
> agents — the `subagent_type: "bugbot"` launch fails there. So this phase pushes + opens the PR
> **first** and relies on the GitHub-App **PR Bugbot**, which reviews every PR update automatically.
> Prerequisite: Bugbot enabled for the repo in the Cursor dashboard; `.cursor/BUGBOT.md` supplies the
> review rules (same rules the local review would use).

1. **Push + PR** — `git push -u origin HEAD`; `gh pr create --base <base branch from your launch prompt>`
   with the `<!-- metadata -->` block (labels, milestone, `Closes #XXX`). Opens the PR and triggers CI +
   the automatic PR Bugbot review once.
2. **PR-Bugbot review** — trigger explicitly with `gh pr comment <pr> --body "bugbot run"`, then wait for
   the `Cursor Bugbot` status check to finish (e.g. `gh pr checks <pr> --watch`). Read findings via
   `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/<pr>/comments` (or `gh pr view <pr> --comments`). Findings → fix via
   refactorer → verifier → tester → commit → push, then re-comment `bugbot run` and re-check until clean.
3. **Final test** — delegate to **tester** ("final test run"): wait on the PHP Quality CI jobs and run
   the Playwright E2E specs in parallel. FAIL → fix via refactorer → verifier → tester, commit, push,
   re-run. (Intermediate fix commits on the open PR may use `[skip ci]`; the last one must not.)
4. **Finalize** (follow `push.mdc`) — branch doc + version bump (once per PR) + `CHANGELOG-NEW.md` +
   ROADMAP closure (incl. PR#), then archive the ticket:
   `git mv migration-docs/tickets/active/{task-slug}_plan.md migration-docs/tickets/done/`. Commit and
   push (second push).
5. **Do not merge** — the user reviews and merges.

